<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
    Notarization requires the hardened runtime, which by default kills the
    process if it marks any memory executable that wasn't loaded from a
    signed file. core-term hits this on the runtime code path traced below --
    NOT at every call site that merely exists in the pixelflow-ir source tree,
    which is a broader (and wrong) standard: pixelflow-compiler's `kernel!`
    macro is proc-macro=true and runs entirely at build time, and
    CompileWorkspace's MAP_JIT pattern (pixelflow-ir/src/backend/emit/mod.rs)
    is only reachable from pixelflow-pipeline's benchmark binaries, which
    core-term does not depend on.

    The path that IS reachable at runtime: rendering a glyph
    (pixelflow-graphics/src/fonts/cache.rs, atlas.rs) calls `.bake(kernel)`,
    which goes through pixelflow_ir::jit_cache::compile_cached /
    compile_collapse_cached -> compile_arena_dag / compile_collapse ->
    ExecutableCode::from_code (pixelflow-ir/src/backend/emit/executable.rs) --
    plain mmap + mprotect(PROT_EXEC), no MAP_JIT. That's what
    allow-unsigned-executable-memory covers; allow-jit is NOT granted here
    because CompileWorkspace's MAP_JIT path is not part of this binary.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
